;; references.sexp — the reference candidate dossier for `dsp56300-lab-v0` (P3-BREADTH.4).
;; One document form; validate with
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py profiles/dsp56300-lab-v0/references.sexp schema/references.sexp
;; Re-derive with `scripts/fetch_references.sh [--verify-only] dsp56300-lab-v0` (needs the
;; network and a Rust toolchain, so it is deliberately NOT a commit gate).

(comment "profiles/dsp56300-lab-v0/references.sexp — the reference candidate dossier for" "`dsp56300-lab-v0`, the bounded DSP56300 subset selected by P3-BREADTH.4 slice 1" "(decision_dsp56300-lab-v0-subset)." "" "⛔ THE SAME RULES AS THE SCALAR DOSSIER APPLY. Every field is an observed fact (SRC-03), an" "`obtained` row was run on this host, and nothing here says the reference is USABLE against a" "Semulith model — `docs/EVIDENCE_AND_GATES.md` §5 makes a matched-profile experiment the gate," "and no Semulith DSP56300 model exists yet. The one experiment row below is the P3-BREADTH.3" "slice-2 demonstration: it exercised the EVIDENCE PATH (pin, build, assemble, run, verify)," "not a model comparison." "" "⚠️ ONE CANDIDATE IS NOT ONE OPINION, and this candidate's own internal legs are recorded in" "the independence rows — assembler and emulator share one project, so the honest independent" "legs are upstream's asm56300 roundtrip and its silicon-sealed difftest corpus, both of them" "upstream proof artifacts Semulith has not re-run (EVD-04).")

(references (profile "dsp56300-lab-v0") (retrieved "2026-10-01") (work_dir "target/refs") (comment "The host is recorded because the candidate was BUILT against its toolchain; on another host" "the same commands can produce a different answer (SRC-03). The repository volume is" "/dev/disk7s1; the shared toolchain prefixes (/opt/homebrew, the rustup store in $HOME) are on" "/dev/disk3s1s1 — DIFFERENT volumes, which is why the build redirects CARGO_HOME and" "CARGO_TARGET_DIR into the repository tree (project data-locality policy).") (host (os "macOS 27.0 (build 26A428)") (kernel "Darwin 27.0.0") (arch "arm64") (cxx "Apple clang 21.0.0 (clang-2100.3.34.2, /usr/bin/clang)") (note "Repository volume /dev/disk7s1; toolchain prefixes on /dev/disk3s1s1. The reference's own build runs under CARGO_HOME=.app-data/cargo-home and CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/refs/dsp56300-build so that every artifact it produces stays on the repository volume.")) (comment "───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── candidate 1: mborgerson/dsp56300" "The oracle survey (P3-BREADTH.3 slice 1) measured this the ONLY DSP family with a complete," "license-clean evidence path; slice 2 exercised the path here end-to-end.") (candidate (id "dsp56300") (role "primary oracle — silicon-validated emulator + assembler, one MIT project") (status "obtained") (kind "source tarball + on-volume cargo build") (origin "https://github.com/mborgerson/dsp56300") (source_commit "c60aeedb6a6014850204c71e53bc0cf5b3104222") (source_authored "2026-09-27") (asset "dsp56300-c60aeedb.tar.gz") (asset_sha256 "46b0e3e532e774859ee59b861901ac53b94a31ca5c924c61f8f32b26d6b308c9") (asset_bytes 643174) (http_status 200) (invocation "dsp56300-asm <guest.a56> -o <guest.lod> -f lod — then — difftest corpus <guest.lod> <case.meta> [--dump-mem] [--dump-stack]; the meta names the case, the load base, the stop pc and the step budget (`case micro 000100 000115 100`).") (trace_granularity "per CASE, end-state canonical dump — NOT a per-instruction trace. Fields: steps, pc sr omr la lc sp ssh ssl ep sz sc vba, x0 x1 y0 y1, a0 a1 a2 b0 b1 b2, r0-r7 n0-n7 m0-m7, cyc (informational only — cycle counts are base-table values, LIMITATIONS §4, and are NEVER compared). --dump-mem appends deviation-encoded X/Y/P windows (X:$0000-$0BFF minus the harness window $0400-$04FF, Y:$0000-$07FF, P:$07C0-$07FF); --dump-stack the 15 hardware stack slots, deviation-encoded against the seed. Comparison is checkpoint-level field-exact equality; the harness is engine-agnostic by its own contract ('anything that can produce the canonical dump format can be compared', tools/difftest/README.md).") (matched_config "none — the emulator models the DSP56300 core as fixed; the experiment's configuration is the corpus CASE (load base, stop pc, step budget, memory init/fill) declared in the meta file, not a model configuration.") (matched_scope "⛔ NOT ESTABLISHED — no matched-profile experiment against a Semulith model has run (none exists). The reference's documented gaps bound every future claim: SA/SC/DM mode bits stored but inert, stack extension unimplemented, cache ops NOPs, pipeline interlocks unmodelled, peripheral-interrupt and fast-vector shapes unverified against hardware (docs/LIMITATIONS.md at the pinned commit, read in full). The subset v0 exclusions map one-to-one onto these gaps (docs/tasks/artifacts/p3-breadth/2026-10-01-subset-selection.md).") (terms "MIT (© 2026 Matt Borgerson) — the LICENSE was re-fetched and read 2026-10-01 (P3-BREADTH.3 slice 1). The tarball is fetched into the untracked target/refs/ working area; no copy is committed and nothing is redistributed.") (lineage "ONE project ships BOTH the assembler and the emulator: one author, one crate workspace. The assembler's independent leg is upstream's exhaustive roundtrip against Motorola's official asm56300 v6.3.15 across the full encoding space; the emulator's independent leg is upstream's difftest corpus compared word-for-word against real MCPX silicon and Motorola's sim56300. Both are UPSTREAM proof artifacts (EVD-04): Semulith has not re-run either — the silicon needs hardware this project does not have, and asm56300/sim56300 are proprietary and unpinnable. The emulator's JIT emitter was additionally early-differential-tested against the xemu/XQEMU DSP56300 core (ARAnyM/Hatari DSP56001 lineage). A second implementation exists (dsp56300/gearmulator, GPL-3.0) and is recorded in the oracle survey as not license-pinnable for this project.") (license "MIT") (build_note "cargo build --release --bin dsp56300-asm --bin difftest under CARGO_HOME=.app-data/cargo-home, CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/refs/dsp56300-build — 31.7 s, green (P3-BREADTH.3 slice 2). Toolchain: the upstream pins 1.98.1 in rust-toolchain.toml; the host's 1.98.0 satisfies the crate's rust-version = \"1.98\" floor and was used via RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.98.0-aarch64-apple-darwin rather than installing 1.98.1 into the OFF-VOLUME rustup store (see the attempt row).")) (comment "───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the build-route deviation, recorded") (attempt (what "build the reference with its upstream-pinned toolchain (rust-toolchain.toml: 1.98.1)") (command "rustup toolchain install 1.98.1") (outcome "DECLINED — the rustup store lives in $HOME, off the repository volume (§13). The host's 1.98.0 satisfies the crate's rust-version = \"1.98\" floor; both tools built and ran green under it.") (consequence "The build is functional but not exact-toolchain-pinned. The exact-toolchain policy for this reference (install on-volume, or re-pin the floor) is an OPEN ITEM owned by this profile's model slice, to be resolved before the reference becomes evidence-bearing rather than path-demonstrating.")) (comment "───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the path demonstration (P3-BREADTH.3 slice 2)" "⚠️ This row records the EVIDENCE PATH exercised, not a matched-profile experiment — no" "Semulith model participated. It is what changed `dsp56300` from a survey row to a path that" "reproduces HERE.") (experiment (id "evidence-path-demo") (program "docs/tasks/artifacts/p3-breadth/dsp56300-demo/micro.a56 (synthetic — evidence about the path, never about any real DSP program)") (instructions 16) (models "dsp56300 (difftest corpus)") (verdict "canonical dump produced headless, rc 0 — pin, build, assemble, execute, dump all green on this host") (expectations "hand arithmetic reproduces the 56-bit accumulator exactly (A = 001f253d515280); --dump-mem shows the X/Y-space stores landing at the right addresses in the right spaces; move #$5,x1 -> x1=050000 traced to DSP56300FM §3.4.1.3 (an 8-bit short immediate to X0/X1/Y0/Y1 is a signed fraction in bits 23-16)") (reproduced "yes — the full record is docs/tasks/artifacts/p3-breadth/2026-10-01-evidence-path-demo.md") (control "the run's one surprising value (x1=050000, not 000005) was treated as a suspected defect and chased to ground truth in the family manual rather than waved through — the natural falsification probe fired and the reference matched the manual")) (comment "──────────────────────────────────────────── the independence inventory (EVD-04)" "⛔ TWO TOOLS WITH DIFFERENT NAMES ARE NOT TWO OPINIONS — and here they do not even have" "different names. Recorded BEFORE any evidence rests on this reference.") (independence (subsystem "assembler vs executor") (pair "dsp56300-asm") (pair "dsp56300-emu (difftest)") (verdict "shared") (evidence "Both live in one repository, one author, one crate workspace (crates/asm, crates/core, crates/emu, tools/difftest) — measured on the pinned source at c60aeedb.") (consequence "Assembly and execution are ONE leg. The encoding's independent confirmation is upstream's asm56300 roundtrip; the semantics' independent confirmation is upstream's silicon-sealed corpus. When Semulith's dsp56300-lab-v0 model exists, its decode and semantics are derived from the pinned family manual — never from this project's decoder tables — precisely so that Semulith-vs-emulator is a second opinion (decision_dsp56300-lab-v0-subset).")) (independence (subsystem "all") (pair "dsp56300 (mborgerson)") (pair "gearmulator (The Usual Suspects)") (verdict "not-examined") (evidence "none — the gearmulator core is GPL-3.0, which this project's pinning discipline does not vendor, and its source has not been read. Recorded in the oracle survey as the family's second implementation.") (consequence "Recorded as unexamined rather than omitted. Nothing in this profile's evidence rests on it; the owner of any future second-oracle claim is the leaf that proposes one, and it must do this examination first.")))
